WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.025
This slide connects Module 2 with what we are doing
now In

00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:09.238
Module 2 we designed the database We created tables
chose data types

00:00:09.388 --> 00:00:14.212
and defined relationships In Module 3 we start using
that structure to

00:00:14.238 --> 00:00:18.375
answer questions and manage rows A helpful habit is
to think of

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:24.100
database work as a short sequence First define the
question For

00:00:24.112 --> 00:00:26.975
example maybe we need a list of active patients who
are at

00:00:26.988 --> 00:00:32.412
least fifty years old Second preview the rows that
match This is

00:00:32.438 --> 00:00:37.838
especially important before changing data Third
protect the operation by using a

00:00:37.862 --> 00:00:43.000
stable key and a clear WHERE condition Fourth
execute the SQL statement

00:00:43.875 --> 00:00:48.800
Finally verify what happened That last step is easy
to skip but

00:00:48.825 --> 00:00:53.488
it is extremely important A query can run
successfully and still produce

00:00:53.512 --> 00:00:57.700
the wrong result if the condition was not what you
intended SQL

00:00:57.725 --> 00:01:02.062
does not know your business meaning It only follows
the instructions you

00:01:02.088 --> 00:01:06.225
write So the core habit for this module is read the
request

00:01:06.412 --> 00:01:10.488
preview the target rows run the smallest correct
statement inspect the result

00:01:10.675 --> 00:01:14.150
and then keep or undo the change You will see this
same

00:01:14.175 --> 00:01:16.275
pattern repeated throughout the module
